%% title: `Ack Reply`
%% summary: Ack legality, ack-state persistence, and delegated reply delivery.
%% commentary: This machine validates the ack target, commits the ack transition first, then builds one reply delivery request and delegates the outward reply path to the approved new-message machine instead of embedding reply logic back into `ack`.
%% notes: ack legality distinct from new-message | reply delegates to NewMessageStateMachine | observable ack-state commit required
%% sets: delivery
flowchart TD
    A["<b>AckReplyStateMachine</b><br/>Received"] --> B["ValidateAckTargetExists"]
    B -->|target_missing| E1["Rejected
validation error"]
    B -->|target_found| C["ValidateReplyTargetAllowed"]
    C -->|reply_rejected| E2["Rejected
validation error"]
    C -->|reply_allowed| D["PersistAckTransition
commit ack-state mutation"]
    D -->|sqlite_err| X["Failed
ack-state persistence failure"]
    D -->|sqlite_ok| F["BuildReplyDeliveryRequest"]
    F --> G["DispatchReplyByHarness
delegate to approved NewMessage machine"]
    G --> O["Delivered"]

    classDef happy fill:#14532d,color:#ffffff,stroke:#14532d,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef error fill:#7f1d1d,color:#ffffff,stroke:#7f1d1d,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef neutral fill:#e2e8f0,color:#111827,stroke:#334155,stroke-width:2px;

    class A,O happy;
    class E1,E2,X error;
    class B,C,D,F,G neutral;
